 logger-console, fs-node, package-manager, loader-utils and create: how ordinary Cordis services are built on the core primitives.","locale":"en"},"7822":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-timer`","locale":"en"},"7823":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-logger-console`","locale":"en"},"7824":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-fs-node`","locale":"en"},"7825":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`@cordisjs/plugin-package-manager`","locale":"en"},"7826":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#loader-utils","content":"`@cordisjs/loader-utils`","locale":"en"},"7827":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"`create-cordis`","locale":"en"},"7828":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"Takeaways for a port","locale":"en"},"7829":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","content":"These packages are not described in the paper; they show how ordinary services are built on the core primitives.","locale":"en"},"7830":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","content":"**Common theme:** every resource is registered through `ctx.effect` on the *calling* fiber (found via the service tracker, see Services and traceability), so it is released when the caller unloads. There is no per-consumer bookkeeping in the service.","locale":"en"},"7831":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`timer/src/index.ts`. Service `timer`, mixed into the context as `ctx.timeout / interval / throttle / debounce / setTimeout / setInterval`.","locale":"en"},"7832":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"API","locale":"en"},"7833":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"Semantics","locale":"en"},"7834":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`timeout(cb, ms) → dispose`","locale":"en"},"7835":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"effect around `setTimeout`; when it fires it first disposes itself (removes the effect from the fiber), then calls `cb`","locale":"en"},"7836":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`timeout(ms) → Promise<void>`","locale":"en"},"7837":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"sleep; disposing the fiber rejects it with `Error('Context has been disposed')`; the effect is removed when the promise settles","locale":"en"},"7838":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`interval(cb, ms) → dispose`","locale":"en"},"7839":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"effect around `setInterval`","locale":"en"},"7840":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`interval(ms) → AsyncIterableIterator`","locale":"en"},"7841":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"each tick resolves only the oldest pending `next()`; ticks without a waiter are dropped; `return()`/`throw()` semantics of async iterators; fiber disposal rejects pending reads","locale":"en"},"7842":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`throttle(cb, ms, noTrailing?)`","locale":"en"},"7843":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"leading call, trailing call with latest args unless `noTrailing`; `.dispose()`","locale":"en"},"7844":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"`debounce(cb, ms)`","locale":"en"},"7845":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#timer","content":"each call restarts the timer; `.dispose()`","locale":"en"},"7846":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"`shared.ts`, `index.ts`, `browser.ts`. A class plugin (`name = 'logger-console'`) whose constructor calls `ctx.logger.exporter(this)`, so the exporter lives exactly as long as the plugin (see Logger).","locale":"en"},"7847":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"Config: `colors` (Node default from `supports-color`), `maxLength`, per-name `levels`, `showDiff`, a `showTime` template, `label { width, margin, align }`.","locale":"en"},"7848":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"It renders a `[E]/[W]/[I]/[D]` prefix, a hashed-colour label, aligned continuation lines and an optional `+Nms` diff; `%o` uses `util.inspect`.","locale":"en"},"7849":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#logger-console","content":"The browser build delegates to `console.*`.","locale":"en"},"7850":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The following describes the historical watcher baseline. Current Rust `fs` additionally supports baseUrl, URL resolution, provider mounts and cancellable read streams, with explicit `fs:local` file reads. See Server auxiliary services for the newer fixed upstream scope.","locale":"en"},"7851":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"`index.ts`, `watcher.ts`. Service `fs`, currently only `watch(path, { filter }) → Watcher`.","locale":"en"},"7852":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"Paths resolve relative to the **caller's** `ctx.baseUrl`; `file:` URLs are accepted; Windows drive-relative forms are rejected.","locale":"en"},"7853":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"A single file is watched **through its parent directory** (`depth: 0`), so atomic rename-based writes do not lose the watch.","locale":"en"},"7854":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The `Watcher` is an async effect wrapping chokidar (`ignoreInitial`), registered after the initial scan. Only `change` events are forwarded; `ready` replays asynchronously to late listeners; dispatch uses a snapshot; listener errors go to `error` listeners (whose own errors are only logged).","locale":"en"},"7855":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#fs-node","content":"The filter consists of gitignore-like rules: **last match wins**, tested against the entry *or any ancestor*. A directory is still traversed if a later including rule's literal base is related; patterns leaving the root are rejected.","locale":"en"},"7856":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`index.ts`, `agent.ts`, `manifest.ts`, `backup.ts`, `process.ts`, `state.ts`. Service `packageManager`: transactional dependency installs driving npm / pnpm / yarn classic / yarn berry (hoisted `node_modules` only).","locale":"en"},"7857":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"`install(changes, { signal })` is serialized:","locale":"en"},"7858":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Detect the agent from `package.json#packageManager` (exact version, verified by `--version`), require a lockfile, and check the layout.","locale":"en"},"7859":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Snapshot the install state and back up the manifest, lockfiles and rc files (mode- and symlink-preserving).","locale":"en"},"7860":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Edit `package.json` (preserving indentation, EOL and sort order).","locale":"en"},"7861":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Run the agent with an **inactivity timeout** and abort support.","locale":"en"},"7862":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Diff the install state (`added/removed/updated`, with real paths).","locale":"en"},"7863":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"On failure: restore the files and run a **non-cancellable recovery install**; if that fails too, throw an `AggregateError`.","locale":"en"},"7864":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Processes are spawned in their own process group (POSIX) and the whole tree is killed (SIGTERM → SIGKILL; `taskkill /T` on Windows). The environment is scrubbed of variables leaked by an outer `yarn run`.","locale":"en"},"7865":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#package-manager","content":"Real paths use Node's JS `realpath` algorithm so that they match module URLs (intended to feed hmr roots; not wired up in the repository).","locale":"en"},"7866":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#loader-utils","content":"`index.ts`, `internal.ts`. `unwrapExports` (ESM/esbuild interop) and `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which gives access to Node's internal cascaded ESM loader (its shape is detected by API presence across Node 22–24.12+). Pure Node glue; **no Rust counterpart**.","locale":"en"},"7867":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"`create/src/index.ts`, `bin.ts`. A standalone scaffolding CLI (it does not use core):","locale":"en"},"7868":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"prompt for a name and prepare the directory;","locale":"en"},"7869":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"fetch the template package (`@cordisjs/boilerplate`) tarball from the configured npm registry and extract it with `strip: 1`;","locale":"en"},"7870":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"optionally stage a pinned Yarn binary (five documented rules);","locale":"en"},"7871":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"rewrite `package.json`, optionally `git init`, install and start.","locale":"en"},"7872":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#create","content":"Errors print a fixed message and `process.exit(1)` (the tests run it as a child process). The `--mirror` flag is parsed but unused.","locale":"en"},"7873":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"timer, fs and the logger exporters are thin wrappers proving that **\"lifetime by effect\" + caller attribution** is enough to make arbitrary resources revertible: exactly the paper's §6.1 acquisition-inside-the-boundary pattern (see Discussion and related work).","locale":"en"},"7874":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-auxiliary#port","content":"package-manager and create are Node-ecosystem tools; for a Rust framework they are optional or must be retargeted (e.g. Cargo / WASM component packages).","locale":"en"},"7875":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"page","content":"Context and reflection","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context","locale":"en"},"7876":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context","content":"How Cordis core represents contexts, stores service bindings per realm, notifies dependents and resolves coeffects through a Proxy.","locale":"en"},"7877":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#context","content":"`Context`: the first-class context","locale":"en"},"7878":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"Construction","locale":"en"},"7879":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"Derivation with `extend()`","locale":"en"},"7880":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#realm-symbols","content":"Realm symbols","locale":"en"},"7881":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`ReflectService`","locale":"en"},"7882":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#impl","content":"`Impl`: a binding","locale":"en"},"7883":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"`provide(name, value?, check?)`: coeffect provision","locale":"en"},"7884":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#set","content":"`set(name, value)`","locale":"en"},"7885":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#get","content":"`get(name, strict = true)` and `_getImpl`","locale":"en"},"7886":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"`notify(names, filter?)`: reactive notification","locale":"en"},"7887":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor` and `mixin`","locale":"en"},"7888":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"Property access through the Proxy","locale":"en"},"7889":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"`locate(ctx, name)`: the committed-view walk","locale":"en"},"7890":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"Interception","locale":"en"},"7891":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"Design observations","locale":"en"},"7892":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/context.ts`, `reflect.ts` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterparts are §3.2 (coeffects, see Reactive coeffects), §5.1.2 (Algorithms 2–3) and §5.1.4 (Algorithm 6), both in Implementation.","locale":"en"},"7893":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#context","content":"`context.ts` declares:","locale":"en"},"7894":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"`new Context()` builds the **root** (`context.ts:36-49`):","locale":"en"},"7895":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It creates empty `isolate`/`intercept` tables (`Object.create(null)`).","locale":"en"},"7896":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It wraps itself in a `Proxy` with `ReflectService.handler`. This proxy *is* the context everybody sees; `this[symbols.root] = self`.","locale":"en"},"7897":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It creates the **root fiber** `new Fiber(self, {}, {}, null, …)` (runtime `null` ⇒ root, uid 0, `ACTIVE`).","locale":"en"},"7898":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It instantiates the four built-in services on the root: `reflect`, `registry`, `events`, `logger`.","locale":"en"},"7899":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#construction","content":"It calls `this.fiber._disposables.clear()`. The built-in mixins and accessors registered during construction are *not* part of the root fiber's revertible effects: they must survive `root.fiber.dispose()`.","locale":"en"},"7900":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`context.ts:55-63`:","locale":"en"},"7901":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"Every derived context is a **prototype-chain child** of its parent. This realizes the paper's *derived realization* (Definition 23): the child overrides some slots and inherits everything else. Nothing needs to be undone; dropping the child object discards the adjustment.","locale":"en"},"7902":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`isolate(name, label?)` (`context.ts:65`) creates `Object.create(this[symbols.isolate])`, sets `shadow[name] = label ?? Symbol(name)` and extends with it. A fresh symbol gives a private realm; a shared `label` gives a shared realm.","locale":"en"},"7903":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"`intercept(name, config)` (`context.ts:73`) follows the same pattern for the intercept table.","locale":"en"},"7904":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"A fiber's context is `parent.extend({ fiber: this })` (`fiber.ts:150`).","locale":"en"},"7905":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#extend","content":"**Key property:** the isolation and interception tables are *prototype chains*. A lookup (`table[name]`) sees the nearest override; `Object.hasOwn(table, name)` detects an isolation boundary introduced at exactly that level (used by `locate`).","locale":"en"},"7906":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#realm-symbols","content":"`ReflectService.provide` lazily assigns a root realm: `ctx[symbols.root][symbols.isolate][name] ??= Symbol(name)` (`reflect.ts:222`). Thus *every* service name has a realm symbol in the root table once it has been provided; isolated contexts override it. The **store is keyed by realm symbol**, which gives the two-layer `k → ρ(k) → σ(ρ(k))` resolution of Definition 24.","locale":"en"},"7907":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`reflect.ts` holds the shared, root-level tables:","locale":"en"},"7908":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"7909":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Paper","locale":"en"},"7910":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7911":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`store: Dict<Impl, symbol>`","locale":"en"},"7912":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"σ (`@@store`)","locale":"en"},"7913":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"realm symbol → current `Impl` (binding)","locale":"en"},"7914":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`props: Dict<Property>`","locale":"en"},"7915":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"–","locale":"en"},"7916":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"declared context properties: `{type:'service'}` or `{type:'accessor', get, set}`","locale":"en"},"7917":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"`_implCounter`","locale":"en"},"7918":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"fresh names","locale":"en"},"7919":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#reflect-service","content":"uid source for `Impl`s (never reused)","locale":"en"},"7920":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#impl","content":"`reflect.ts:65-75`:","locale":"en"},"7921":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"`reflect.ts:213-249`. `provide` is a `fiber.effect` (therefore tracked and revertible) whose callback:","locale":"en"},"7922":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"registers or validates `props[name]` as a service (an error if it is already an accessor);","locale":"en"},"7923":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"ensures a root realm symbol and computes `key = ctx[isolate][name]`;","locale":"en"},"7924":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"performs the **single-source check**: it throws `service \"x\" has been registered at <fiber>` if `store[key]` exists (O-Insert's disjointness, per realm);","locale":"en"},"7925":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"sets `store[key] = impl` and `fiber.provisions.add(impl)`;","locale":"en"},"7926":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"if the providing fiber is already `ACTIVE`, calls `notify([name])` immediately; otherwise notification happens when the fiber becomes `ACTIVE` (`Fiber._updateState`), matching \"only Active fibers provide\".","locale":"en"},"7927":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"Its **inverse** is async:","locale":"en"},"7928":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"delete the store entry (if it still holds this impl) and `notify` dependents in the impl's realm;","locale":"en"},"7929":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"the **provider-side guard**: `await` until `impl.dependents` is empty (`impl.release` is resolved by the last dependent's unload). It always yields at least once, so child cleanup can still access the inherited service;","locale":"en"},"7930":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#provide","content":"remove the impl from `fiber.provisions`.","locale":"en"},"7931":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#set","content":"`reflect.ts:200-211`. An in-place overwrite of the *own* binding (`impl.value = value`); an error if the name is not provided or is provided by another fiber. There is **no notification**: as the paper notes, an in-place overwrite is not observed by dependents.","locale":"en"},"7932":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#get","content":"`reflect.ts:188-198`. Resolves `ctx[isolate][name]` → `store[key]`. In `strict` mode it returns nothing unless `impl.ctx.fiber.state === ACTIVE` (**provider availability = Active**). It never throws.","locale":"en"},"7933":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"`reflect.ts:251-270`:","locale":"en"},"7934":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#notify","content":"This is Algorithm 3. The *filter* parameter exists so that the loader can replace the realm test during realm reassignment (Algorithm 7, see Managed realms).","locale":"en"},"7935":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor(name, {get, set})` and `mixin(source, keys)` live at `reflect.ts:272-308`.","locale":"en"},"7936":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`accessor` declares a computed context property (as a revertible effect).","locale":"en"},"7937":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`mixin('events', ['on', 'emit', …])` exposes members of a service as context properties (`ctx.on` → `ctx.events.on`) bound to the accessing context. It is a generator effect that yields one accessor per key.","locale":"en"},"7938":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"The root wires (`reflect.ts:182-185`):","locale":"en"},"7939":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"7940":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"Keys mixed into the context","locale":"en"},"7941":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`reflect`","locale":"en"},"7942":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`get`, `set`, `provide`, `accessor`, `mixin`","locale":"en"},"7943":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"7944":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`runtime`, `effect`","locale":"en"},"7945":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`registry`","locale":"en"},"7946":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`inject`, `plugin`","locale":"en"},"7947":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`events`","locale":"en"},"7948":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#accessor-mixin","content":"`on`, `once`, `parallel`, `emit`, `serial`, `bail`, `waterfall`","locale":"en"},"7949":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"`ReflectService.handler` (`reflect.ts:105-170`) mediates `ctx.foo` in its `get` trap:","locale":"en"},"7950":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"*special* properties (symbols, `prototype`, `then`, numeric strings, names starting with `_`) bypass mediation;","locale":"en"},"7951":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"ordinary own or inherited properties are returned through `getTraceable` (see Services and traceability);","locale":"en"},"7952":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"a declared **accessor** → its getter;","locale":"en"},"7953":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"if the *def site* (the shadow, see Services and traceability) is the **root fiber** → unchecked `reflect.get(prop, false)` (root code cannot declare `inject`);","locale":"en"},"7954":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"otherwise a `waterfall('internal/get', …)` (which lets plugins hook access) around `locate(defSite, prop)`:","locale":"en"},"7955":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"impl found → its value (traced);","locale":"en"},"7956":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"the fiber declares the key but has no committed impl → `cannot get required service \"x\" in inactive context`;","locale":"en"},"7957":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-81","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"nobody declares it → `cannot get property \"x\" without inject`.","locale":"en"},"7958":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-82","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"The `set` trap: an undeclared property on a non-root fiber → the error `cannot set property without provide`; an accessor → its setter; a service → `waterfall('internal/set')` → `reflect.set`.","locale":"en"},"7959":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-83","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#proxy","content":"Errors are created as cheap placeholders and only materialized with a trimmed stack when thrown (`createAccessError`/`enhanceAccessError`).","locale":"en"},"7960":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-84","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"`reflect.ts:83-102` implements Algorithm 6, extended with own provisions and isolation boundaries:","locale":"en"},"7961":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-85","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"Consequences, all covered by `tests/isolate.spec.ts` and `reflect.spec.ts`:","locale":"en"},"7962":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-86","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"a consumer reads the **committed** impl, not the live store, so it keeps seeing its dependency during its own teardown (Theorem 70);","locale":"en"},"7963":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-87","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"a child plugin *inherits* the injection of an ancestor (`inject` declared on an ancestor admits access in descendants);","locale":"en"},"7964":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-88","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#locate","content":"an isolation boundary stops inheritance (`does not inherit the injected view across isolation boundaries`).","locale":"en"},"7965":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-89","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"`Service[symbols.resolveIntercept]` (`service.ts:57-70`) resolves the metadata for a service named `name` at access time:","locale":"en"},"7966":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-90","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"walk the context's intercept prototype chain, collecting own values **outer → inner**;","locale":"en"},"7967":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-91","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"prepend the *component-declared* metadata `locate(caller, name).fiber.inject[name]` (the value given in `inject: { name: meta }` of the declaring fiber) at the lowest priority. There is none for own provisions, and the walk stops at an isolation boundary;","locale":"en"},"7968":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-92","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"merge with `service[symbols.mergeIntercept]` (default `Object.assign({}, ...values)`, so right-biased).","locale":"en"},"7969":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-93","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#interception","content":"This is exactly `σ(k)(d(k) ⊕ ι(k))` from Definition 27, with ⊕ = shallow object merge (customizable per service). The `logger` service uses it for `{ name, level }` (`logger.ts:213-224`).","locale":"en"},"7970":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-94","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Everything is in the root.** There is one `store`, one `props` and one `registry` per root; derived contexts differ only by their prototype-chained `isolate`/`intercept` tables and their `fiber`. This keeps \"is key k provided in realm r?\" a single map lookup.","locale":"en"},"7971":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-95","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Provider identity** is the `Impl.uid`, a fresh counter value. This implements the \"name, not value\" discipline of the committed and target views.","locale":"en"},"7972":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-96","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**Isolation per realm symbol** implements the relaxed calculus \"disjoint within a realm\" (§4.4, see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"7973":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-context-97","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-context","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-context#design-observations","content":"**No compile-time checking**: declared vs. accessed keys are checked only at runtime, by the proxy (paper §5.1.4 notes this could be static).","locale":"en"},"7974":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"page","content":"Effects","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","locale":"en"},"7975":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","content":"How Cordis core tracks revertible effects: accepted shapes, the execution engine, fiber.effect, ownership transfer and teardown order.","locale":"en"},"7976":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Accepted effect shapes","locale":"en"},"7977":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"The engine `_execute(runner)`","locale":"en"},"7978":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`fiber.effect(execute, label)`: the tracked effect","locale":"en"},"7979":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#ownership","content":"Nesting and ownership transfer","locale":"en"},"7980":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`DisposableList`","locale":"en"},"7981":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Fiber-level accumulator vs. the paper","locale":"en"},"7982":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Error handling summary","locale":"en"},"7983":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"Tests documenting the semantics","locale":"en"},"7984":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/fiber.ts:60-363` and `utils.ts`. The paper counterpart is §3.1 and Algorithm 1; see Revertible effects.","locale":"en"},"7985":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"`fiber.ts:64-76`:","locale":"en"},"7986":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"An effect callback may therefore return:","locale":"en"},"7987":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Callback returns","locale":"en"},"7988":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Paper reading","locale":"en"},"7989":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a function","locale":"en"},"7990":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"an effect function 𝔈Γ (the returned function is the inverse)","locale":"en"},"7991":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"`undefined`/`null`","locale":"en"},"7992":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"identity effect (nothing to undo)","locale":"en"},"7993":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a `Promise<function>`","locale":"en"},"7994":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"async effect function","locale":"en"},"7995":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"a sync generator yielding disposers","locale":"en"},"7996":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"effect iterator ℑΓ, run to completion synchronously","locale":"en"},"7997":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"an async generator yielding disposers","locale":"en"},"7998":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"effect iterator with **iteration boundaries** that check a guard","locale":"en"},"7999":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#shapes","content":"Anything else throws `TypeError('Invalid effect')`.","locale":"en"},"8000":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`fiber.ts:240-290`. `EffectRunner { epoch, execute, collect, getOuterStack }` abstracts the two users of the engine, a single `ctx.effect` call and a fiber's whole `apply`:","locale":"en"},"8001":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`execute()` produces the effect value;","locale":"en"},"8002":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`collect(dispose)` records a yielded inverse;","locale":"en"},"8003":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`epoch` is the **guard**. For async iterators the loop runs `while (runner.epoch === oldEpoch)`; when the epoch changes, the loop stops after the current iteration lands and `iter.return()` is called so the generator's `finally` blocks run (`fiber.ts:269-285`).","locale":"en"},"8004":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"**Sync iterators are not interruptible** (there is no guard check); they could not be interrupted anyway in a single-threaded host. Every `collect` is type-checked (`safeCollect`).","locale":"en"},"8005":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#execute","content":"`composeError(…, getOuterStack)` stitches the error stack together with the stack captured where the effect or plugin was *created* (`buildOuterStack`). This produces long stack traces that point at the user's `ctx.plugin(...)`/`ctx.effect(...)` call site. It is pure DX and JS-specific.","locale":"en"},"8006":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`fiber.ts:292-357`. `ctx.effect` is `ctx.fiber.effect` (mixed in by `ReflectService`). Step by step:","locale":"en"},"8007":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`assertActive()`: a fiber whose `uid` is `null` (removed) cannot create effects (`CordisError('INACTIVE_EFFECT')`).","locale":"en"},"8008":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"A local list `disposables` and a local `dispose()` that runs them **in reverse order**. If one returns a promise, the remaining ones are chained after it (sequential LIFO, `fiber.ts:298-311`).","locale":"en"},"8009":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`EffectMeta { label, children }` for introspection (`fiber.getEffects()`, used by tooling).","locale":"en"},"8010":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"A runner whose `epoch` is a boolean (`armed` in Algorithm 1) and whose `collect`:","locale":"en"},"8011":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"pushes the disposer into the local list,","locale":"en"},"8012":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"**removes it from the fiber's top-level list** (`this._disposables.delete(dispose)`), an ownership transfer (see below),","locale":"en"},"8013":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"records child metadata.","locale":"en"},"8014":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Execute. On a synchronous throw, dispose what was collected and rethrow.","locale":"en"},"8015":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Async failures: `task.catch(dispose)`. A failing async effect rolls back what it collected, and errors are logged rather than left unhandled.","locale":"en"},"8016":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"Build the returned **wrapper** (the disposer):","locale":"en"},"8017":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"at-most-once (`epoch` flips to `false`), Theorem 7's soundness invariant;","locale":"en"},"8018":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"flipping `epoch` also stops an in-flight async iterator at its next boundary;","locale":"en"},"8019":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"if setup is still running, disposal waits for it first (`task.then(dispose)`).","locale":"en"},"8020":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`wrapper.then(...)` makes the disposer **awaitable**: `await ctx.effect(...)` waits for setup to finish and resolves to a disposer.","locale":"en"},"8021":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#fiber-effect","content":"`disposables.push(this._disposables.push(wrapper))`: the wrapper is registered in the **fiber's** list, and the function that removes it from that list is the first local disposable (so disposing an effect manually also unregisters it from the fiber).","locale":"en"},"8022":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#ownership","content":"Calling `ctx.effect` inside another effect's callback first registers the inner wrapper in the fiber's list. If the outer callback **yields or returns** that wrapper, `collect` moves ownership: the wrapper leaves the fiber's list and becomes part of the outer effect. If it is not yielded, it stays a direct child of the fiber. This implements the paper's \"parent composition\" (`ctx.dispose ← dispose ∘ ctx.dispose`) *without* nesting effect scopes: the accumulator of a fiber is the `DisposableList` `fiber._disposables`.","locale":"en"},"8023":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`utils.ts:5-40`. An insertion-ordered `Map<number, T>` plus a `WeakMap<T, number>`:","locale":"en"},"8024":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`push(v)` returns a remover `() => map.delete(sn)`;","locale":"en"},"8025":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`delete(v)` removes by identity;","locale":"en"},"8026":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"`clear()` returns the values **reversed** (LIFO) and empties the list.","locale":"en"},"8027":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#disposable-list","content":"It is used for fiber disposables, runtime fiber lists and per-fiber hook lists. It is an instance of the \"insert with fresh id, remove by id\" commutative-key design from paper §3.4.2 (see The context paradigm).","locale":"en"},"8028":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"The fiber's accumulator is not one composed closure but the list `fiber._disposables`. On unload (`fiber.ts:488-498`):","locale":"en"},"8029":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Disposers are **initiated in reverse order but run concurrently**; each starts after a microtask. Inside a single effect they are sequential LIFO. The paper acknowledges this (\"`fiber.dispose` initiates a fiber's effects concurrently\", §5.1.3), and it is sound under the independence results (Theorem 43: inverses of independent effects can run in any order; see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"8030":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#accumulator","content":"Ordered teardown *within* one logical effect must therefore be expressed by grouping it in one `ctx.effect` (a generator).","locale":"en"},"8031":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Situation","locale":"en"},"8032":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"8033":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"sync throw in effect callback","locale":"en"},"8034":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"collected disposers run, error rethrown to caller","locale":"en"},"8035":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"async rejection in effect","locale":"en"},"8036":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"collected disposers run, error logged","locale":"en"},"8037":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"invalid yielded value","locale":"en"},"8038":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"`TypeError('Invalid effect')`","locale":"en"},"8039":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"error in a disposer during fiber unload","locale":"en"},"8040":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"logged; other disposers still run (`tests/fiber.spec.ts: 'dispose error'`, `service-dispose.spec.ts: 'releases dependencies after a cleanup error'`)","locale":"en"},"8041":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"effect on removed fiber","locale":"en"},"8042":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#errors","content":"`CordisError INACTIVE_EFFECT`","locale":"en"},"8043":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`tests/dispose.spec.ts` covers:","locale":"en"},"8044":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`dispose by plugin`, `dispose manually`, `yield dispose`;","locale":"en"},"8045":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async return 1/2`, `async yield 1`;","locale":"en"},"8046":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield 2/3 (aborted)`: disposing during setup stops the generator and disposes only what was yielded;","locale":"en"},"8047":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield (aborted, finally)`: `finally` runs;","locale":"en"},"8048":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`async yield 4 (await dispose)`;","locale":"en"},"8049":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-effects-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-effects#tests","content":"`return/yield with error`, `async yield invalid effect`.","locale":"en"},"8050":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"page","content":"Events and logger","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events","locale":"en"},"8051":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events","content":"Cordis's EventsService (registration as an effect, dispatch modes, internal events) and its logger (name resolution, levels, exporters).","locale":"en"},"8052":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#events","content":"`EventsService`","locale":"en"},"8053":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"Storage and registration","locale":"en"},"8054":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Dispatch modes","locale":"en"},"8055":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#internal-events","content":"Internal events","locale":"en"},"8056":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#logger","content":"Logger","locale":"en"},"8057":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-events#port","content":"Observations for a port","locale":"en"},"8058":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/core/src/events.ts` and `logger.ts`. In the paper, event listeners are the canonical *commutative key* (\"registration takes an entry of its own\", §3.4.2, see The context paradigm); the logger is an example of interception metadata.","locale":"en"},"8059":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#events","content":"`events.ts`. There is one instance on the root, mixed into contexts as `ctx.on/once/emit/parallel/serial/bail/waterfall`.","locale":"en"},"8060":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`_hooks: Record<name, Hook[]>` with `Hook { ctx, callback, prepend?, global?, removed? }`.","locale":"en"},"8061":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`on(name, listener, options)` (`events.ts:187-200`):","locale":"en"},"8062":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`assertActive()` on the calling fiber;","locale":"en"},"8063":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`listener = ctx.reflect.bind(listener)`: arguments and `this` are traced to the listener's context;","locale":"en"},"8064":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`bail('internal/listener', name, listener, options)` lets special events take over registration (used for the per-fiber `internal/update`);","locale":"en"},"8065":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"otherwise `register()`: a **`fiber.effect`** that pushes or unshifts the hook and returns `unregister` (which marks `removed = true`, splices, and deletes empty buckets). Because `this.ctx` is the traced use-site context, the effect is owned by the *listener's* fiber (see Services and traceability).","locale":"en"},"8066":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#registration","content":"`once` disposes itself before calling the listener, so recursive emits and concurrent serial dispatches run it once.","locale":"en"},"8067":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`events.ts:110-163`:","locale":"en"},"8068":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Mode","locale":"en"},"8069":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"Semantics","locale":"en"},"8070":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`emit`","locale":"en"},"8071":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"synchronous, all listeners, return ignored","locale":"en"},"8072":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`parallel`","locale":"en"},"8073":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`Promise.allSettled`; failures aggregated into `AggregateError`","locale":"en"},"8074":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-events-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-events#dispatch","content":"`serial`","locale":"en"},"8075":{"id":