notification happens when the fiber becomes `ACTIVE` (`Fiber._updateState`), matching \"only Active fibers provide\"."],[6877,"if the transaction itself fails, all its files are retried, and the error is logged as a warning;"],[8419,"If this is not the first read: a three-way **reconcile** of the journal against the old and new file states; the **file wins** on conflict, and each conflict is logged."],[7955,"impl found → its value (traced);"],[6633,"Implement `Guest` and `export!` it:"],[5776,"Implementation"],[5177,"Implementation as described by the paper (Algorithms 1–10), loader, HMR, Koishi"],[7714,"Implementation as described in the paper: Algorithms 1–10, loader, HMR, Koishi (§5)"],[4710,"Implementation in the paper"],[5178,"Implementation in the paper"],[5727,"Implementation phases"],[5728,"Implementation status"],[8092,"implementation swapped"],[5552,"Implemented in `registry.rs` (`warn_cycle`): a depth-first search along \"depends on a declared provider\" edges, logging `dependency cycle: a -> b -> …` at warning level."],[7117,"Implementing `Plugin`"],[8625,"Implications for the Rust port"],[4561,"Important consequences:"],[6832,"imports `name` and returns its plugin; fails with `module <name> does not export a plugin` otherwise"],[6830,"imports a module and its dependencies, dependencies first, and caches them. In a cycle, a module that is still being imported is seen as `Exports::None`. A module that fails to load is not kept, so its next import tries again."],[8574,"imports the module and patches the context;"],[5254,"In `kardia-core` (`root.rs`), the root is the private `RootInner { state: Mutex<State>, changed: Notify, logger: Mutex<LoggerState> }`. A critical section is `RootInner::run(|st: &mut State| …)`: it pushes `Action`s onto `State::actions` instead of returning them. The actions are `Reload(FiberId)` and `Unload(FiberId)` (spawn the transition), `Emit(..)` (deliver an event to listeners), `Log { .. }` (report an error through the logger) and `Drop(..)` (values released under the lock are dropped after it, since their destructors are user code). Instead of per-action `Wake(Notify)`, every critical section wakes all waiters on the root-wide `changed` notifier after unlocking. Disposers are not run as an action: the unload transition runs them itself, outside the lock (see Lifecycle algorithms)."],[8151,"In `registry.ts`, a **plugin** (the paper's *component*) is one of:"],[6409,"in a plugin's `apply`, once its load has been superseded or the fiber retired (the paper's L-Divert)"],[4937,"In a purely functional setting the two coincide; an imperative host may choose per operation. **Isolation and interception are given derived realization**: they produce a child context whose own table differs from the inherited one, leaving the shared table untouched, so there is nothing to track. Assignment on a derived table overrides the inherited one at that key, so neither operation has a precondition."],[4988,"In all cases loading is an effect whose inverses undo the registrations the module introduced."],[4879,"In an async host, iterations and inverses are futures that run to completion once started, so the **aborting** alternative of L-Divert is unavailable. Such a host is **inertial**: a fiber whose target turns during an iteration deactivates after that iteration lands. All results quantify over all runs, so they cover inertial runs; Theorem 73 never uses the aborting alternative. Inverses in flight need no counterpart (Unloading is never declined). A deactivation may chain directly back into an activation (implementation: `reload`/`unload` mutual chaining, see Implementation in the paper)."],[6411,"in an effect body, once the effect has been disposed"],[7461,"In configuration files, isolation is the entry field `isolate` (`{ db: true }` for a private realm, `{ db: shared }` for a realm shared under a label); see The loader."],[8561,"in place"],[5456,"In the code (`effect.rs`, `fiber.rs`):"],[5501,"In the code (`events.rs`): `trait Event: Any + Send + Sync { type Output: Bailable; fn filter(&self, listener: &Context) -> bool { true } }`. `Bailable` (implemented for `()`, `bool`, `Option<T>` and `Result<T, Error>`) says which results stop a `bail` / `serial` dispatch and which count as failures of a `parallel` one. `filter` replaces `E: Scoped`: `ServiceChanged` reaches only listeners whose context resolves the key to the same realm. Listeners are kept in a `Vec` per `TypeId`. `on` returns `Result<EffectHandle>`; there are also `on_prepend`, `on_async`, `once` and `listener_count`. The hooks are `ctx.on_config(..)` (config transform), `ctx.on_update::<C>(..)` (update hook per fiber), and the `ConfigCommitted` event as the commit point. `ConfigCommitted` carries `{ fiber, config }`. `serial` returns `Result<Option<E::Output>>`: a panicking listener stops it with the panic as the error, while `emit` and `bail` log a panicking listener, synchronous or asynchronous, and continue (see Events)."],[5495,"In the code (`fiber.rs`): `context()` returns `&Context`. `settled()`, `restart()` and `fail(error)` return a `Settle` (a boxed future of `kardia_core::Result<()>`), `dispose()` a `Disposal` (a future of `Result<()>`; disposing the root fiber restarts it, reverting everything registered on it), and `update(config)` / `update_with(config, no_save)` a `Result<Settle>`. There are also `config()`, `inject()`, `error()`, `runtime()`, `def()`, `name()`, `parent()`, `is_removed()`, `is_root()`, `effect_handle()` and `effect_count()`. `ctx.fiber()` returns the fiber of a context."],[5597,"In the code (`graph.rs`): `trait ModuleSource: Send + Sync + 'static { fn load(&self, id: &str) -> Result<ModuleCode>; }`. `ModuleId` is a `String` (an absolute path), `ModuleCode { deps: Vec<ModuleId>, evaluate }` evaluates against its dependencies' exports, and a module exports `Exports::{None, Plugin(PluginDef), Value(Value)}`. `ModuleGraph::new(source)` keeps an ordered table of loaded records (`deps`, `exports`) and the set of host modules."],[5507,"In the code (`logger.rs`): `ctx.logger()` takes no name (it is named by `intercept(\"logger\", { name })` or after the fiber's plugin), `ctx.logger_named(name)` names it explicitly, and `svc.logger()` logs on a caller's behalf. Levels are `error`, `warn`, `info` and `debug`, and each takes `impl Display`, so `format_args!(..)` works directly. Exporters are registered with `ctx.add_exporter(Arc<dyn Exporter>)`, an effect of the current fiber; `Exporter::export(&Message)` and an optional per-name `level`. `Message` is `{ sn, ts, name, level, text, fiber }`: the text is already formatted (see Logger). The buffer holds 1000 messages by default (`ctx.log_buffer()`, `ctx.set_log_buffer_size(n)`). No `tracing` bridge has been added."],[5474,"In the code (`plugin.rs`, `registry.rs`):"],[5541,"In the code (`state.rs` and `fiber.rs`), `FiberState` and `Target` are as sketched, except that `Target::Epoch::providers` is a `Vec<ImplId>` (the workspace does not use `smallvec`). `FiberData` differs:"],[5432,"In the code there is neither a `Meta` type nor `Mergeable` / `Intercepted`. Interception metadata stays JSON: `trait Service: Any + Send + Sync { const NAME: &'static str; fn merge_intercept(values: Vec<Value>) -> Value { merge_shallow(values) } }`, where the values come outermost first and the default is a right-biased shallow merge of JSON objects. A service reads typed metadata with `ctx.intercept_meta::<T>(key)`. `#[derive(Service)]` (from `kardia-macros`) implements the trait; `#[service(name = \"database\")]` sets the key, which defaults to the hyphenated type name."],[5992,"In the code, `ctx.checkpoint()` and `scope.yield_(d)` are synchronous checks (`ctx.checkpoint()?`, `scope.yield_(d)?`), not futures; the decision itself (no dropped `apply` futures, divert at explicit boundaries) holds. The `TypeId` of D3 is not stored with the binding: a key collision surfaces as `AccessError::TypeMismatch` when the stored `Arc<dyn Any>` fails to downcast."],[5485,"In the code, `Fiber::update(value)` and `Fiber::update_with(value, no_save)` return `Result<Settle>`: validation errors are returned at once, and the `Settle` future resolves when the update has taken effect (`db.update(json!(..))?.await?`). The update hook is `ctx.on_update::<C>(|new: &C| -> bool)` (returning `true` takes the update over, no restart) or `ctx.on_update_with::<C>(..)` (returning the future that `update` resolves with); `C` is the plugin's decoded configuration type. Before a plugin's own decoding, the configuration passes through the root's config hooks (`ctx.on_config(..)`), which the loader uses to evaluate expressions."],[5439,"In the code, `provide` and `provide_arc` return `kardia_core::Result<EffectHandle>` (the error is `kardia_core::Error`, which wraps `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided` and the other variants). Further variants: `provide_as` / `provide_arc_as` (any value under an explicit key), `provide_checked` (with an availability predicate) and `provide_serialized_as` (a value with a JSON view for expressions and tooling). `ctx.replace_value` was not implemented: `KardiaError::NotProvided` and `ForeignBinding` are declared for it but no API returns them. Retiring a provider unbinds its live provisions at once (see Retired providers)."],[5595,"In the code, `serde_json::Value` has no expression variant: `!!js` becomes the object `{ \"__jsExpr\": \"…\" }` (`kardia_loader::EXPR_KEY`). Errors are `ConfigFileError` / `ConfigIssue` values whose locations are `file:line:col`, and the loader prints located frames as text (`at <id> (file:line:col)`) rather than a `ConfigFrame` type; see Errors."],[5454,"In the code, `Svc<T>` holds the value `Arc<T>`, the caller `Context`, the `key`, the `impl_id` and the providing fiber, with `caller()`, `key()`, `impl_id()`, `arc()`, `provider()` and `logger()`. `intercept()` is `meta() -> Value` (merged with `S::merge_intercept`) and `intercepts() -> Vec<Value>` (the unmerged list, declared `inject` metadata first). The timer's `TimerExt::timeout` returns `Result<EffectHandle>` and registers `self.caller().effect_sync(\"ctx.timeout()\", …)`. Service-to-service calls follow the def site, unlike TS (see Service-to-service calls)."],[5534,"In the code, a `Scope` is one node of a context's derivation chain: `Scope { parent: RwLock<Option<Arc<Scope>>>, kind: ScopeKind }`, with `ScopeKind::{Fiber(FiberId), Isolate(Key, RealmId), Intercept(Key, Value), Overlay(Arc<Overlay>)}`. Every derived context (a fiber's own context, `isolate`, `intercept`, `extend`) adds a node; re-pointing a parent moves everything below it. The loader's mutable per-entry tables are public `Overlay` nodes (`set_isolations`, `set_intercepts`), and the entry marker is an `Overlay::tagged(tag)` found again with `Context::tag()`. Because scope nodes carry their fiber, the fiber chain of an access is read off the derivation chain (see Re-pointable contexts)."],[5536,"In the code, both structs live in `state.rs`:"],[5494,"In the code: `ctx.registry().replace(&old_def, &new_def) -> Vec<Fiber>` returns the fibers moved to the new definition, and each moved fiber emits `Replaced`."],[5449,"In the code: `get` and `AccessError` are as sketched. `try_get_live` is `live::<S>()` (and `live_as::<T>(key)`); `get_dyn` is `get_as::<T>(key)` for a typed value under a name, and `view(key)` for the JSON view of a service, which the loader's expressions use. Typed declarations use the `Deps` trait (implemented with `macro_rules!` for tuples of up to eight services): `Inject::of::<(Database, Cache)>()` builds the runtime declaration, and `ctx.deps::<(Database, Cache)>()` returns `(Svc<Database>, Svc<Cache>)`. `Plugin` has no `Inject` associated type; it declares with `fn inject() -> Inject`. The compile-time step is `Injected<D>`, used by `#[plugin]` (see Checked typed access)."],[5532,"In the code: `Key`, `RealmId`, `ImplId` and `FiberId` exist as sketched (`FiberId::ROOT` is `0`, `RealmId::new()` creates a fresh realm). `RealmId` prints as `realm#n`; the readable labels `svc#id` / `svc@label` belong to the loader's realms. There is no `EffectId`: effects are `EffectCell`s held in an `IdTable`, whose ids are plain `u64`."],[6544,"in the host process"],[6200,"In the parent group's context"],[6872,"In watch mode, `hmr` watches the directory at the scoped `fs.baseUrl` and turns file changes into transactions:"],[7087,"In YAML, `!!js <source>` reads as an expression object `{ \"__jsExpr\": source }` and is written back the same way. Unknown tags are errors, since they would leave the data incomplete. Written YAML uses block style, with single-quoted strings where needed."],[5438,"In-place overwrite (`reflect.set`) is offered as `ctx.replace_value::<S>(..)` and, as in Cordis and the paper, is *not* observed by dependents."],[1592,"include"],[3933,"include"],[4519,"include"],[6106,"include"],[8447,"include"],[9033,"include"],[8449,"include (internal)"],[5888,"include `sync.spec`, `patch.spec`, `reload.spec`, `write.spec` (fault injection on rename), `parse.spec`; fs `watch.spec`"],[1374,"include `sync.spec`、`patch.spec`、`reload.spec`、`write.spec`（在重命名时注入故障）、`parse.spec`；fs `watch.spec`"],[5756,"include + fs specs green; editing `kardia.yml` live reconfigures a running app"],[7723,"Include and group"],[8372,"Include and group"],[1242,"include 与 fs 的 spec 通过；编辑 `kardia.yml` 能实时重新配置正在运行的应用"],[3209,"include 与分组"],[3858,"Include 与分组"],[2579,"include 在值的所有者写它的地方定位它：在自己的文件中，或在父文件中的某个补丁里；"],[3938,"include 是论文中配置与纤程（fiber）之间*双向*绑定最清晰的例子：运行时变更（插件自我更新或自我禁用、API 编辑）流回文件，文件编辑流入纤程，冲突以确定性的方式解决。"],[8375,"Include: a file-backed `EntryTree`"],[3861,"Include：以文件支撑的 `EntryTree`"],[3935,"include（内部）"],[1297,"include（配置文件引入）在值的所有者写下它们的地方定位这些值（所有者的文件，或其父级文件中的一个补丁），别名定位到其锚点，表达式中的字符穿过 YAML 转义定位。运行时更改的值不会被定位。`Entry::evaluate` 未公开。"],[6890,"Including config files"],[4651,"Independence (§3.4.1)"],[4674,"Independence is needed for two situations Theorem 16 does not cover: running an inverse while *later* effects are still in place (removing one component of a running system), and interleaving the effects of several components."],[6041,"inertia"],[5237,"Inertia"],[8671,"Inertia"],[5625,"inertial host + explicit checkpoints (Interruption)"],[5718,"Initial FS Windows acceptance found NotFound for a file used as a parent path, versus Unix NotADirectory. Native expectations were corrected and CI #43700024799 passed; error mapping was not hidden."],[5042,"Initialization-time DI"],[5279,"Inject faults into the real implementation and verify all three policies: automatic retry without test code calling recovery APIs, remaining failed until explicit handling in manual mode, and following the host's decision while containing handler failures in custom mode. Continuously check unrelated plugins under every policy, repeat failures to verify cleanup, and verify that disposal cancels pending recovery. Validate the relevant native platforms separately."],[8543,"inner fiber ctx"],[5287,"Inside a package, modules import each other by absolute path: `import { Fiber } from \"#/fiber\"`. `#/` is a subpath import, mapped in each `package.json` (`\"imports\": { \"#/*\": { \"source\": \"./src/*.ts\", \"types\": \"./lib/*.d.ts\", \"default\": \"./lib/*.js\" } }`). Node, TypeScript and bundlers resolve it per package, so the published `lib/` works as `tsc` emits it; type checking and tests resolve it to the sources through the `source` condition (`customConditions` in `tsconfig.json`, `ssr.resolve.conditions` in `vitest.config.ts`). The `@/` alias of `site/` would not survive into a published package, since `tsc` does not rewrite path aliases."],[5463,"Inside one effect: disposers run **sequentially in reverse order**."],[6513,"inspection"],[5327,"Install Rust **1.99.1** (`dtolnay/rust-toolchain@1.99.1`) with `rustfmt`, `clippy` and the `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target. The toolchain is pinned because the compile-error snapshots of `kardia-macros` (trybuild tests) depend on the compiler version."],[7753,"Install the binary"],[7749,"Installation"],[7744,"Installation, then Writing plugins, Services, Effects and Guest plugins"],[6441,"Instantiates"],[5422,"Instantiation (O-Insert / O-Retire)"],[5224,"Instantiation `⟨d, p, e, π, σ, τ, θ⟩` (parent, own table, retirement flag, lifecycle state)."],[8677,"Instantiation as parent effect"],[8139,"Instantiation: O-Insert and O-Retire"],[8294,"Integration"],[8113,"intercept listener registration"],[8110,"intercept property access (used by loader/isolate tooling)"],[7890,"Interception"],[4939,"Interception attaches cross-cutting **metadata** to dependency access without changing the value."],[7443,"Interception attaches metadata to a key along a context chain, so that a service can behave differently per caller (paper Def. 26–27). The usual example is the logger: `logger: { name: db, level: 3 }` renames and re-levels the logger of everything below."],[4956,"Interception merge"],[8686,"Interception merge"],[5215,"Interception metadata"],[7315,"Interception metadata"],[5453,"Interception metadata is resolved at access time per Def. 27 / `resolveIntercept`: `[declared inject meta, outer…, inner]` merged right-biased."],[7441,"Interception metadata of the outer caller does not reach the services a service calls in turn; it stays on `Svc::caller()`."],[7645,"Interface composition: settings sections, commands, renderers, panels"],[5841,"Internal events"],[8055,"Internal events"],[5500,"Internal events: `PluginInserted/Removed`, `StatusChanged { fiber, old, new }`, `ServiceChanged { key, realm }`, `ConfigCommitted { fiber, value }`, `Replaced { fiber }`."],[5554,"Internals of kardia-loader, kardia-include and kardia-hmr: the Rust adaptations of the Cordis loader, the file-backed include and the hot-reload algorithm with its module backends."],[5039,"Interposed reclamation"],[5982,"Interruption"],[5417,"Interruption and cancellation safety (D6)"],[7244,"Introspection"],[8037,"invalid yielded value"],[6008,"inver