ices on the root: `reflect`, `registry`, `events`, `logger`."],[8389,"It is a class plugin whose async-generator `[Service.init]` reads the file, yields `() => this.stop()`, and applies the tree. Its entries' composite ids are `<includeEntryId>:<localId>`; includes nest."],[7602,"It is a port of Kardia's core rather than a wrapper of the TypeScript Cordis:"],[8027,"It is used for fiber disposables, runtime fiber lists and per-fiber hook lists. It is an instance of the \"insert with fresh id, remove by id\" commutative-key design from paper §3.4.2 (see The context paradigm)."],[8160,"it moves every fiber of the old runtime to the new runtime via `fiber._replace(runtime, inject)`."],[5354,"It publishes every crate whose new version is not on crates.io yet, in dependency order (`cargo publish --workspace`; `xtask` is never published), then creates a GitHub release for the tag, with notes since the previous `v*` tag."],[5364,"It publishes with **npm trusted publishing**: the publish job's `id-token: write` permission lets it mint a short-lived OIDC token that npm accepts for packages whose trusted publisher names this repository and workflow. No npm token is stored anywhere, and npm attaches a provenance statement to each version automatically (this needs the repository to stay public)."],[5359,"It publishes with the `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` repository secret."],[8159,"it records an alias `old → new`, so later `ctx.plugin(old)` instantiates `new` (aliases are followed in chains and can switch back);"],[7848,"It renders a `[E]/[W]/[I]/[D]` prefix, a hashed-colour label, aligned continuation lines and an optional `+Nms` diff; `%o` uses `util.inspect`."],[8320,"It requires Node's internal ESM loader (`loader-utils` → `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which needs `--expose-internals` or the `node-addon-require-builtin` addon); the constructor throws otherwise (fiber FAILED, no service)."],[7371,"It stays `Pending` until every declared service is available, then loads."],[7399,"I