t as modules in the graph, mark them with `graph.mark_host(ids)`. A change to a host module is not applied; it is reported in `ReconcileResult::skipped_host_modules`, and watch mode warns:"],[5036,"Statically scoped reversal"],[5725,"Status and deviations"],[8729,"Status in the code"],[4847,"Steps are indexed by `t`; `step^t = r(n)` is the rule applied and the fiber it acts on. Runs start from an empty registry. An **episode** of `n` is a maximal interval during which `installed_n` holds; it opens just after an L-Begin and closes at an L-Unload. Every step factors as `γ^{t+1} = edit^t(Ψ^t(γ^t))`; tables (`σ_m`) move only inside `Ψ`, control fields (`θ, τ, π, d, p, e`, the registry domain) only inside `edit` (except through instantiation). States are compared with a `≃` that keeps all control fields (eq. 54)."],[5037,"STM, reversible computing (Janus), RCCS, linear types, **RAII, Rust ownership**"],[522,"STM、可逆计算（Janus）、RCCS、线性类型、**RAII、Rust 所有权**"],[5443,"stop at an isolation boundary;"],[7124,"Stopping cleanly"],[7510,"stops the dispatch: `serial` returns `Err(..)` with the panic, and later listeners do not run"],[7240,"Stops the plugin and removes it"],[6158,"Stops the plugin without removing its entry."],[8053,"Storage and registration"],[8256,"store the config and clear `_error`;"],[6233,"Streaming HTTP and WS echo"],[6289,"string"],[6313,"string"],[5636,"string keys can collide; `TypeId` unstable across dylibs"],[6018,"string name / `any`"],[8775,"String paths support parameters, wildcards, optional groups and quoted parameter names, following path-to-regexp 8.4.2. Path captures decode percent escapes and preserve literal `+`. Queries preserve duplicate keys and still decode `+` as a space. `Path::regex(source, flags)` uses ECMAScript syntax with g/y state, UTF-16 matching and Unicode flags. Intercept prefixes use string-prefix matching without an extra segment-boundary rule."],[6095,"structured error types"],[7679,"Suggested reading order"],[5698,"Supplement /