pendency holder + the inner plugin)."],[4689,"Two registrations name two entries; either order answers every test alike; each can be withdrawn while the other stands. (The same reason CRDTs tag every addition uniquely.)"],[7570,"Two runtimes, one model"],[5110,"Two things are deliberately **left out** here and supplied later by *independence* (§3.4, see The context paradigm): reverting out of the order the accumulator imposes, and sequences that interleave the effects of other components."],[8683,"Two-layer isolation"],[6281,"Type"],[6309,"Type"],[6334,"Type"],[5635,"Type-level keys"],[5448,"Typed declarations: `Plugin::Inject` can be a tuple of service types (`(Database, Cache)`), implemented with `macro_rules!` over tuples, producing both the runtime `InjectSpec` and a typed accessor `ctx.deps::<P::Inject>() -> Result<(Svc<Database>, Svc<Cache>)>`. This is the first, macro-free step towards the compile-time mediation the paper suggests (§5.1.4, §6.4)."],[5426,"Typed events"],[6061,"typed events: `trait Event` + `ctx.on::<E>()`, dispatch modes"],[6529,"Typed failures"],[8885,"typed handles obtainable only via declared injection"],[7568,"TypeScript and Tauri"],[4095,"TypeScript Cordis 代码在哪些地方遵循论文的模型与伪代码、在哪些地方偏离或细化了它、发现的缺陷，以及 Rust 移植遵循哪一方。"],[6252,"TypeScript package"],[7646,"TypeScript plugins on `@kardiajs/core`"],[1219,"TypeScript 一侧"],[3054,"TypeScript 与 Tauri"],[1738,"TypeScript 包"],[3057,"TypeScript 运行时"],[7919,"uid source for `Impl`s (never reused)"],[6181,"unary `!`, `-`, `+`; arithmetic `+ - * / %`;"],[5685,"Unavailable upstream"],[4598,"unchanged"],[8733,"unchecked, a provider obligation (stated in the paper)"],[8731,"unchecked, an author obligation (stated in the paper)"],[4592,"undefined"],[4603,"undefined"],[4645,"Unified context (§3.3.1)"],[5168,"Unified context, coeffect operations, observational equivalence, independence, commutativity"],[5860,"Unit tests"],[7249,"Unknown fields are tolerated, unless the config type opts into `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`."],[6500,"Unless `no_save` is set, `ConfigCommitted { fiber, config }` is emitted (the loader writes it back to the config file)."],[4802,"Unlike `ctx.get` (which never fails), the proxy resolves against the accessing fiber's **committed view** and enforces the specification at the point of use. Reading the view rather than the store is what keeps a dependency readable during the consumer's own teardown (Theorem 70). The check is made at runtime but, since `inject` is static, could be made at compile time (§6.4, for example with Rust procedural macros or traits; see Discussion and related work)."],[7514,"Unlike Cordis, `emit` does not let a failing listener abort the dispatch, and there is no generic `waterfall`: extension points that Cordis builds on waterfall events are typed hooks (below)."],[7105,"Unlike the TypeScript loader, the new isolation table is installed together with the re-parenting at the end of the chain, not before the hooks run."],[8567,"unload / reload"],[4899,"Unload waits for dependents (guard)"],[4817,"unload when set, reload when cleared"],[6438,"Unloading a parent cascades to its children: each child plugin is an effect of its parent, so the parent's unload disposes them."],[7238,"Unloads and loads a non-failed plugin again; a failed plugin stays failed"],[8343,"Unrelated plugins are untouched. Different fibers reload concurrently (a slow drain does not delay a fast plugin)."],[8805,"Unset; inline / attachment are supported"],[4813,"update in place (consulted at read time; no reload)"],[6363,"Update, restart and dispose"],[8261,"updates during unloading coalesce;"],[7133,"Updating `db`'s config restarts it. `greeter` depends on it, so `greeter` stops first and starts again with the new database."],[5691,"Upstream comparisons live in the standalone `.github/workflows/server-reference.yml` workflow for manual verification. Select **Server reference → Run workflow** in GitHub Actions to run the Linux, Windows and macOS matrix. Its only t